Have you considered multivariate analyses (e.g., NMDS, PCA, PLSDA, etc)? Regarding your approach, it seems like conducting so many tests in one experiment would increase the likelihood of making Type I errors.  There are various ways to correct for this (e.g., Bonferroni correction). Maybe someone more knowledgeable could provide guidelines for when and how to deal with this issue?

